            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous origins of left anterior descending and circumflex coronary arteries from separate orifices in the right coronary sinus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>373-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is described of a 69-year-old man with angina pectoris who was found at coronary angiography to have all three coronary arteries arising by separate orifices from the right coronary sinus. This appears to be a previously unreported anomaly. The embryological origin and mechanisms of angina in coronary arterial anomalies are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
